    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a potent lineup anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who projects as our premier start with an 81.88 efficiency score. Despite facing Seth Lugo\u2014a pitcher who historically suppresses stolen base attempts\u2014**Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park-factor boost (+16%) and a strong platoon advantage, making him our most reliable engine for counting stats. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.23) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) also stand out as high-floor plays, with both benefiting from favorable matchups against starters with xERAs above 5.00. **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** are critical components as well; **Kyle Tucker** in particular carries a high 75.35 score, thriving despite the lefty-on-lefty matchup due to his elite offensive profile, while **Andy Pages** benefits significantly from facing Bratt, who provides an excellent opportunity for power production.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Miguel Vargas**, who landed on the bench with a 56.21 score. Despite maintaining an elite xwOBA of 0.403, **Miguel Vargas** was squeezed out of the starting nine by the higher aggregate efficiency scores of our middle-infield starters. Similarly, **Brayan Rocchio** (56.28) was a strong consideration but ultimately fell short of the threshold required to displace our current starters against their respective opponents. On the risk front, we are monitoring **Liam Hicks** (43.11) closely; his score is dragged down by a double-digit penalty for a dynamic platoon disadvantage against Cantillo. While we remain confident in the overall offensive output, we are mindful of the \"slow delivery\" caveats for **Josh Lowe** and **Jackson Merrill**, as those factors provide a marginal boost to their stolen base potential despite the high-caliber arms they are facing today.",
